 (list type)←GetOpenProjects;listCider;listAcre
⍝ Returns all opened Cider and acre projects that are Git-managed: a matrix with the name of
⍝ the namespace in [;1] and the folder in [;2]. When both managers contribute there is a third
⍝ column saying which project came from which.\\
⍝ `type` tells where they come from: 1=Cider, 2=acre, 3=both, 0=none. That is what
⍝ `SelectProject` needs in order to get its caption right.\\
⍝ When the global `∆OPEN_PROJECTS` exists it is returned instead, with `type` 3. That is a seam
⍝ for the test suite: it allows a test case to define what "open" means without opening or
⍝ closing anything, so a test run does not depend on what the user happens to have open, and
⍝ does not disturb it either.
 :If 2=⎕NC'∆OPEN_PROJECTS'
     (list type)←∆OPEN_PROJECTS 3
     :Return
 :EndIf
 listCider←⎕SE.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0
 :If AcreIsAvailable
     listAcre←⎕SE.acre.Projects 0
 :Else
     listAcre←0 2⍴⍬
 :EndIf
 :If 0∧.<≢¨listCider listAcre
     list←(listCider,⊂'(Cider)')⍪listAcre,⊂'(acre)'
 :Else
     list←listCider⍪listAcre
 :EndIf
 list←(F.IsDir(F.AddTrailingSep¨list[;2]),¨⊂'.git')⌿list
 type←{2=+/⍵:3 ⋄ 0=+/⍵:0 ⋄ ⊃⍵/1 2}0<≢¨listCider listAcre
⍝Done
